X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=openbsd-alpha&m=101696896629100

Hi,

I just fixed a very serious bug on alpha that affected almost all pci
machines (except my main development machine).

So, if you have ever experienced instability on your alpha and random
crashes, especially under high concurrent dma and interrupt load (many
people say that disabling soft updates helped, which should lower
the amount of interrupts that happen during setting up dma), you might
want to test the latest snapshots that are out on the ftp servers now.

//art
