X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=openbsd-alpha&m=101631368501162

Hiya,

did anyone ever netboot a multia (latest SRM, 3.8-3) successfully? If yes,
how?
after switching to bootp the second stage bootloader is successfully
retrieved. That's where the problems start. The machine's MAC address has to
be hardcoded in the bootloader (according to the netbsd/alpha FAQ, and
indeed is doesn't work without). So I used the netbsd bootloader and
hardcoded the machine's mac. The second stage bootloader then issues another
bootp/dhcp request to get its IP and stuff, and there it fails, it never
sees the reply. I've read that may be a unicast/multicast issue. I'm using
the OpenBSD dhcpd. I'm out of ideas. 

Greetz

Henning

