From openbsd-alpha  Tue Mar 12 17:12:32 2002
From: Patrick Giagnocavo <patrick () zill ! net>
Date: Tue, 12 Mar 2002 17:12:32 +0000
To: openbsd-alpha
Subject: Re: AlphaServer 400
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=openbsd-alpha&m=101595341028477

Load averages are not a useful measure of system activity.

Try either

iostat -d -C 1

for a continuous listing of disk and CPU activity, or

vmstat 5 

for a listing of several useful kernel stats.

The man pages for each command are of course useful.

./patrick
